  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2304.02 Display of Decals",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2304.02 Display of Decals.\n\n(a) Each registration decal issued by the department shall:\n\n(1) Be displayed within 6 inches to the right of the vessel number;\n\n(2) Be clearly visible on each side of the vessel and within 2 feet of the stem, if the vessel is exempt from displaying a vessel number pursuant to RSA 270-E:9, II; or\n\n(3) Be displayed within 6 inches to the right of the vessel number or clearly visible on the port and starboard facing portion of the windshield, if an antique or classic vessel.\n\n(b) Each boat fee decal shall be displayed directly next to the registration decal.\n\n(c) The registration decal and boat fee decal shall be displayed only on the vessel to which it was issued.\n\nSource. #5283, eff 11-22-91; ss by #6616, eff 10-25-97, EXPIRED: 10-25-05\n\nNew. #8506, INTERIM, eff 12-7-05, EXPIRES: 6-5-06; ss by #8617, eff 4-28-06, EXPIRED: 1-21-15 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 2300)\n\nNew. #10787, eff 2-20-15; ss by #14321, eff 7-16-25, EXPIRES: 7-16-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2300.html"
